---
import OfferLayout from "../layouts/OfferLayout.astro";
const path = "/agency-pitch-doctor";
const breadcrumb = [
  { label: "Home", href: "/" },
  { label: "Agency Pitch Doctor", href: path },
];
const faqs = [
  { q: "What is pitch consulting for agencies?", a: "Outside senior help to win new business: pitch strategy, deck surgery, rehearsal and war-gaming the procurement process. I work alongside your team in the run-up to a pitch to sharpen the story and the delivery." },
  { q: "How do you help win a pitch?", a: "I find the through-line that makes the pitch coherent, cut the slides that dilute it, pressure-test the numbers, and rehearse the room until the team can hold their nerve. Most pitches are lost on clarity and conviction, not on capability." },
  { q: "When should we bring you in?", a: "As early as possible, ideally at the strategy stage rather than the week before. I can still help with late-stage deck surgery and rehearsal, but the biggest gains come from shaping the narrative before the deck exists." },
  { q: "What's your track record?", a: "I led the strategy and pitch that won a 13-market Gucci account at Assembly, and led major pitches at Medialab. I have sat on the agency side of enterprise pitching and know how procurement actually decides." },
  { q: "Do you work with agencies that compete with each other?", a: "I take one agency per live pitch to avoid conflicts, and I am explicit about it. Your strategy stays yours." },
];
---
<OfferLayout
  title="Agency Pitch Doctor"
  eyebrow="For agencies"
  lead="New-business and pitch consulting for agencies: pitch strategy, deck surgery, rehearsal and war-gaming procurement. I have won the big ones."
  description="Pitch consulting for agencies: strategy, deck surgery, rehearsal and procurement war-gaming, from someone who led a winning 13-market Gucci pitch. Tom Goodwin, Founder of GAMEPLAN."
  {path}
  serviceName="Agency Pitch Consulting"
  breadcrumb={breadcrumb}
  faqs={faqs}
  ctaHeading="Got a pitch you can't afford to lose?"
  ctaBody="Tell me what you're pitching for and when. I'll tell you honestly whether I can help you win it."
>
  <p><strong>I help agencies win the pitches that matter.</strong> Pitch strategy, deck surgery, rehearsal and war-gaming the procurement process, from someone who has led winning pitches at the enterprise tier. When the brief is worth a year of revenue, the margin between winning and losing is preparation.</p>

  <h2>Who this is for</h2>
  <p>Agency leaders and new-business teams heading into a pitch they need to win: a defence, a major prospect, a competitive review. Especially useful when your team is strong on craft but the story is not landing, or when procurement is part of the decision and nobody has war-gamed it.</p>

  <h2>What you get</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A pitch narrative with a clear through-line, not a feature list</li>
    <li>Deck surgery: cut what dilutes, sharpen what convinces</li>
    <li>Rehearsal until the team can hold the room under pressure</li>
    <li>Procurement war-gaming: the questions and the numbers, anticipated</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Proof anchor</h2>
  <p>I led the strategy and pitch that won a 13-market Gucci account at Assembly, and led major pitches as Search Director at Medialab. This is a category with almost no specialist competition, because few people have actually won at this level and will sit with your team to do it again.</p>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Read.</strong> The brief, the incumbent, the panel, the real decision criteria.</li>
    <li><strong>Sharpen.</strong> Narrative, deck and numbers, cut to what wins.</li>
    <li><strong>Rehearse.</strong> War-game the room until delivery is second nature.</li>
  </ol>
</OfferLayout>
